    {
      "id": 262873,
      "name": "MindWanderer",
      "username": "MindWanderer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
      "created_at": "2025-03-20T17:47:55.409Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Escher\" data-post=\"6\" data-topic=\"31425\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/escher/48/4865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Escher:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>He’s fully aware that there is no Egyptian afterlife, because that’s where his bunch came from and it’s a dead hell dimension now. Like, in the Sentinels lore, all the Egyptian religious beliefs are misunderstandings (intentionally or not) of the powers of extradimensional beings, right?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Only sort of. The Egyptian afterlife realm is still a real place, and some dead spirits still go there. <a href=\"https://sentinelswiki.com/index.php/Podcasts/Episode_267\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">As can the living.</a> So, if anything, he should have <em>more</em> respect for the Egyptian afterlife rituals than mundane Egyptians.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2025-03-20T17:47:55.409Z",
      "reply_count": 1,
      "reply_to_post_number": 6,
      "quote_count": 1,
