    {
      "id": 265194,
      "name": "",
      "username": "LonelyMan",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2026-03-05T21:22:25.244Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I think Soothsayer Carmichael would respect Rambler, post his time working for a Gloomy; and would be likely to grow to like him if they interacted for a while.  Given the forces Rambler contends with, he kinda doesn’t have the option of doing it too wrong OR not wrong at all; he has to gamble, and I feel like Cedric would see what he’s doing and with who, and go “if you have to have contact with these things at all, then twisting the word of your bargain with them is really your only option.”  So he’d have a grudging admiration despite not fully approving.  I think they could be bros.  Likely they never canonically meet, but I kinda want them to.</p>\n<p>Really pleased with Adam’s answer to the mummy question.</p>\n<p>Wager Master would totally do a Guise lookalike contest.</p>\n<p>These guys are forgetting their own lore; they said they didn’t expect to live to 2351, when it’s already been established that Christopher will upload his brain to a computer so he’ll never truly die,vehicle Adam will die but the Cult of Gloom IPAs he’s been drinking for years will rouse his dread spectre from the grave, essentially becoming a visual art equivalent of Grimm, and then he and Christopher.mp7 will just keep doing the podcast until the end of turn.  (Obviously Trevor will also need to be involved somehow, but I’m not sure what his “thing” will be, since both mad science and dark magic are taken.)</p>",
